<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
<include>prompts/torus_rust.prompt</include>
Output src/z2_gauge.rs. Exact enumeration of Z2 lattice gauge theory. satisfied_plaquette_histogram(torus,twisted:&[bool])->Option<Vec<u128>>: N_j = number of link configurations with exactly j plaquettes satisfying s_p*sigma_p=+1 (s_p=-1 on twisted plaquettes); Gray code, one link flip per step, update only the plaquettes of that link's coboundary; None if twisted has wrong length or links > MAXIMUM_ENUMERATED_LINKS (28). Module doc MUST state Z[twist](beta)=sum_j N_j exp(-2 beta (P-j)). binomial(n,k)->Option<u128>. two_dimensional_histogram_closed_form(side,odd_number_of_twists): N_j = 2^P*binomial(P,j)*(1+sign*(-1)^(P-j)), P=side^2, with the character-expansion derivation in the doc comment. No floating point. Independent tests: tests/z2_enumeration.rs (closed form L=2,3; totals 2^links; twist-move invariance, mono-notes Lemma ym:lem:twist-move; 3D 2x2x2 twist nontrivial; 2^10 flat configurations).
